  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tournons la Page coalition in Niger is an integral part of the &quot;Let&apos;s Turn the Page&quot; campaign, an international citizen movement present in Africa and Europe, promoting alternation and good democratic practices. created in 2014, Tournons is currentlypresentedin 8 African countries (Burundi, Cameroon, Congo-Brazzaville, Gabon, DRC, Chad, Niger-and Ivory Coast) and in Europe. It has more than 220 member organizations and partners with many powerful and legitimate NGOs (Secours Catholique-Caritas France, Misereor, Amnesty International, Front Line Defender, ACAT, Survival, etc.).
In Niger, Tournons la Page&apos;s national coalition brings together 14 human rights organizations, labor unions, women, youth, journalists and artists. The number of activists through the structures is estimated at 3000, distributed in all regions, departments and communes of Niger. TLP Niger has also developed a strategic partnership of mobilization with certain local partners such as the Confederation of Workers of Niger (CNT),the General Confederation of Workers of Niger (CGT-Niger) and the Collective of Organizations for the Defense of Human Rights. Man and Democracy (CODDHD)

The national coalition of Tournons La Page Niger is also attached to the international coordination of TLP. As a technical body hosted by Secours Catholique-Caritas France in Paris, the international coordination assists all national coalitions, including the Nigerien coalition, in carrying out its activities. It did away with the know-how and skillsof Catholic secrets to assist actors in the field on theiradvocacy activities. International coordination also plays a role in the internal sharing of information and practices of TLP members and the defense of members in the event of a physical, judicialor psychological threat.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tournons La Page Niger</narrative>
